@INDEX
MS-DOS command help

APPEND     Makes selected directories available to programs.
ASSIGN     Redirects one drive to another.
ATTRIB     Displays or changes file attributes.
BACKUP     Backs up files.
BREAK      Controls extended CTRL+C checking.
CALL       Calls another batch program.
CD         Displays or changes the current directory.
CHCP       Displays or changes the active code page.
CHDIR      Displays or changes the current directory.
CHKDSK     Checks a disk and displays a report.
CHOICE     Prompts for a key and returns its choice number.
DELTREE    Deletes a directory tree.
CLS        Clears the screen.
COMMAND    Starts a command interpreter.
COMP       Compares two files or sets of files.
COPY       Copies files.
CTTY       Changes the controlling terminal.
DATE       Displays or sets the date.
DEBUG      Tests and edits programs.
DEFRAG     Reorganizes files to improve disk performance.
DEL        Deletes files.
DIR        Displays files and directories.
DISKCOMP   Compares two floppy disks.
DISKCOPY   Copies one floppy disk to another.
DOSKEY     Recalls commands and defines macros.
ECHO       Displays messages or controls command echoing.
EDLIN      Starts the line editor.
EMM386     Controls the expanded-memory manager.
ERASE      Deletes files.
EXE2BIN    Converts an executable file to binary format.
EXIT       Exits the command interpreter.
EXPAND     Expands compressed distribution files.
FASTOPEN   Speeds access to frequently opened files.
FC         Displays differences between files.
FDISK      Manages disk partitions.
FIND       Searches for a text string.
FOR        Repeats a command for items in a set.
FORMAT     Formats a disk.
GOTO       Transfers batch execution to a label.
GRAFTABL   Loads extended characters for graphics mode.
GRAPHICS   Loads graphics-screen printing support.
HELP       Displays command help.
IF         Performs conditional batch processing.
INCLUDE    Includes another CONFIG.SYS configuration block.
INTERLNK   Displays or changes the Interlnk client connection.
INTERSVR   Shares drives through an Interlnk transport.
JOIN       Joins a drive to a directory.
KEYB       Configures a national keyboard.
LABEL      Creates or changes a volume label.
LOADFIX    Loads a program above the first 64K of memory.
LH         Loads a program into upper memory.
LOADHIGH   Loads a program into upper memory.
MD         Creates a directory.
MEM        Displays allocated and free memory.
MEMMAKER   Optimizes conventional and upper-memory use.
MENUCOLOR  Sets startup-menu text and background colors.
MENUDEFAULT Selects a startup-menu default and timeout.
MENUITEM   Adds a choice to a CONFIG.SYS startup menu.
MKDIR      Creates a directory.
MIRROR     Records disk information for recovery.
MODE       Configures system devices.
MORE       Displays output one screen at a time.
MOVE       Moves files or renames files and directories.
MSCDEX     Installs the CD-ROM redirector.
MSD        Displays system diagnostic information.
SCANDISK   Checks and repairs FAT12 and FAT16 disks.
NLSFUNC    Loads country-specific information.
PATH       Displays or sets the program search path.
PAUSE      Suspends batch processing.
PRINT      Prints text files in the background.
POWER      Controls the resident power-management driver.
PROMPT     Changes the command prompt.
RD         Removes an empty directory.
RECOVER    Recovers readable data from a damaged disk or file.
REN        Renames files.
RENAME     Renames files.
REPLACE    Replaces destination files.
RESTORE    Restores files created by BACKUP.
RMDIR      Removes an empty directory.
SET        Displays or changes environment variables.
SETVER     Displays or changes the DOS version table.
SHARE      Installs file sharing and locking support.
SMARTDRV   Configures and reports the disk cache.
SHIFT      Shifts batch parameters.
SORT       Sorts input.
SUBST      Associates a path with a drive letter.
SUBMENU    Adds a nested CONFIG.SYS startup menu.
SYS        Transfers system files to a disk.
TIME       Displays or sets the time.
TREE       Displays a directory tree.
TYPE       Displays a text file.
UNDELETE   Restores files deleted with DEL.
UNFORMAT   Restores a disk erased by FORMAT.
VER        Displays the MS-DOS version.
VERIFY     Controls disk-write verification.
VOL        Displays a volume label and serial number.
XCOPY      Copies files and directory trees.

Type HELP command for syntax, or command /? for detailed help.
@APPEND
Makes files in selected directories available as if they were current.
Syntax: APPEND [drive:]path[;...] [/X[:ON|OFF]] [/PATH:ON|OFF] [/E]
@ASSIGN
Redirects drive references to another drive.
Syntax: ASSIGN [drive1=drive2 ...] [/STATUS]
@ATTRIB
Displays or changes file attributes.
Syntax: ATTRIB [+R|-R] [+A|-A] [+S|-S] [+H|-H] [filespec] [/S]
@BACKUP
Backs up files from one disk to another.
Syntax: BACKUP source target [options]
@BREAK
Controls extended CTRL+C checking.
Syntax: BREAK [ON|OFF]
@CALL
Calls one batch program from another.
Syntax: CALL batchfile [arguments]
@CD
Displays or changes the current directory.
Syntax: CD [drive:][path]
@CHDIR
Displays or changes the current directory.
Syntax: CHDIR [drive:][path]
@CHCP
Displays or changes the active code page.
Syntax: CHCP [nnn]
@CHKDSK
Checks a disk and displays a status report.
Syntax: CHKDSK [drive:][[path]filename] [/F] [/V]
@CHOICE
Prompts for one key from a selectable list and returns its one-based position.
Syntax: CHOICE [/C[:]choices] [/N] [/S] [/T[:]choice,seconds] [text]
@DELTREE
Deletes directories, their files, and all subdirectories.
Syntax: DELTREE [/Y] [drive:]path [[drive:]path ...]
@CLS
Clears the screen.
Syntax: CLS
@COMMAND
Starts a new command interpreter.
Syntax: COMMAND [[drive:]path] [device] [/E:nnnn] [/P] [/C command] [/K command] [/D] [/F] [/MSG] [/Y]
At startup, F5 or Shift bypasses CONFIG.SYS and AUTOEXEC.BAT; F8 confirms each line.
@COMP
Compares the contents of two files or sets of files.
Syntax: COMP data1 [data2] [/D] [/A] [/L] [/N=number] [/C]
@COPY
Copies one or more files.
Syntax: COPY [/A|/B] source [/A|/B] [+ source ...] [destination] [/A|/B] [/V] [/Y|/-Y]
Prompts before replacing files unless /Y or COPYCMD=/Y selects automatic replacement.
@CTTY
Changes the terminal device used to control the system.
Syntax: CTTY device
@DATE
Displays or sets the date.
Syntax: DATE [date]
@DEBUG
Runs the program testing and editing tool.
Syntax: DEBUG [[drive:][path]filename [arguments]]
@DEFRAG
Reorganizes files on a FAT12 or FAT16 disk.
Syntax: DEFRAG [drive:] [/F [/S[:]order] | /U] [/B] [/SKIPHIGH]
              [/LCD | /BW | /G0] [/H]
/U makes file chains contiguous. /F also requests free-space compaction and
/S selects directory order. /H includes hidden files.
@DEL
Deletes files.
Syntax: DEL [drive:][path]filename [/P]
@DIR
Displays files and subdirectories.
Syntax: DIR [drive:][path][filename] [/P] [/W] [/A[:attributes]] [/O[:sort]] [/S] [/B] [/L]
@DISKCOMP
Compares two floppy disks.
Syntax: DISKCOMP [drive1: [drive2:]] [/1] [/8]
@DISKCOPY
Copies one floppy disk to another.
Syntax: DISKCOPY [drive1: [drive2:]] [/1] [/V]
@DOSKEY
Edits command lines, recalls commands, and creates macros.
Syntax: DOSKEY [/REINSTALL] [/BUFSIZE=size] [/MACROS] [/HISTORY] [macro=[text]]
@ECHO
Displays messages or controls batch-command echoing.
Syntax: ECHO [ON|OFF] or ECHO message
@EDLIN
Starts the line-oriented text editor.
Syntax: EDLIN [drive:][path]filename [/B]
@EMM386
Controls the installed EMM386 expanded-memory manager.
Syntax: EMM386 [ON|OFF|AUTO] [W=ON|W=OFF]
@ERASE
Deletes files.
Syntax: ERASE [drive:][path]filename [/P]
@EXE2BIN
Converts an executable file to binary format.
Syntax: EXE2BIN [drive:][path]input-file [[drive:][path]output-file]
@EXIT
Exits the current command interpreter.
Syntax: EXIT
@EXPAND
Expands a compressed distribution file.
Syntax: EXPAND source [destination]
@FASTOPEN
Improves access time for frequently opened files.
Syntax: FASTOPEN drive:[[=]entries] [...] [/X]
@FC
Compares files and displays their differences.
Syntax: FC [/A] [/C] [/L] [/LBn] [/N] [/T] [/W] file1 file2
@FDISK
Creates, displays, selects, or deletes disk partitions.
Syntax: FDISK
@FIND
Searches for a text string.
Syntax: FIND [/V] [/C] [/N] [/I] "string" [[drive:][path]filename ...]
@FOR
Runs a command for each item in a set.
Syntax: FOR %variable IN (set) DO command
@FORMAT
Formats a disk for use with MS-DOS.
Syntax: FORMAT drive: [/V[:label]] [/Q] [/U] [/C] [/S] [/F:size] [/1] [/4] [/8] [/B]
/C retests clusters already marked bad; otherwise FORMAT preserves their marks.
@GOTO
Transfers batch execution to a label.
Syntax: GOTO label
@GRAFTABL
Loads a table of extended characters for graphics mode.
Syntax: GRAFTABL [codepage] [/STATUS]
@GRAPHICS
Loads support for printing graphics screens.
Syntax: GRAPHICS [printer-type] [profile] [/B] [/R] [/LCD] [/PRINTBOX:STD|LCD]
@HELP
Displays help for MS-DOS commands.
Syntax: HELP [command]
@IF
Performs conditional processing in batch programs.
Syntax: IF [NOT] condition command
@INCLUDE
Includes another named CONFIG.SYS block at this position.
Syntax: INCLUDE=blockname
@INTERLNK
Displays or changes the installed Interlnk client connection.
Syntax: INTERLNK [client[:]=[server][:]]
Load INTERLNK.EXE with DEVICE in CONFIG.SYS to mount up to five server volumes.
Options: /DRIVES:n (0-5), /NOPRINTER, /COM:n (1-4), /BAUD:rate, /AUTO, /NOSCAN, /LOW, and /V.
/DRIVES:0 installs only printer redirection and consumes no client drive letter.
/NOSCAN installs offline; /AUTO installs only when startup discovery succeeds.
DEVICE prefers upper memory when available; /LOW keeps the client conventional.
An empty server name cancels that client-drive mapping. /RECONNECT is a repository extension.
@INTERSVR
Shares a DOS volume with an Interlnk client over COM1.
Syntax: INTERSVR [drive: ...] [/X=drive: ...] [/COM:n] [/BAUD:rate] [/B] [/V]
COM ports 1 through 4 are supported.
Use /B for monochrome output and /V for timer-safe polling.
With no drive list, all available drives except those named by /X are shared.
The server remains active while the client reads and writes the shared volume.
@JOIN
Joins a disk drive to a directory on another drive.
Syntax: JOIN drive: [drive:]path or JOIN drive: /D
@KEYB
Configures a keyboard for a language.
Syntax: KEYB [xx[,[yyy][,[drive:][path]filename]]] [/E] [/ID:nnn]
@LABEL
Creates, changes, or deletes a disk volume label.
Syntax: LABEL [drive:][label]
@LOADFIX
Loads a child program above the first 64K of conventional memory.
Syntax: LOADFIX [drive:][path]filename [arguments]
@LH
Loads a program into upper memory.
Syntax: LH [drive:][path]filename [arguments]
@LOADHIGH
Loads a program into upper memory.
Syntax: LOADHIGH [drive:][path]filename [arguments]
@MD
Creates a directory.
Syntax: MD [drive:]path
@MEM
Displays allocated and free memory.
Syntax: MEM [/CLASSIFY|/DEBUG|/FREE|/MODULE name|/PAGE]
@MEMMAKER
Optimizes startup files so drivers and resident programs use upper memory.
Syntax: MEMMAKER [/B] [/BATCH|/CUSTOM] [/SESSION] [/FINAL] [/SWAP:drive] [/T]
                [/UNDO] [/W:size1,size2]
/BATCH selects unattended defaults. /SESSION completes the reboot pass.
/UNDO restores the byte-exact CONFIG.SYS and AUTOEXEC.BAT backups.
@MENUCOLOR
Sets startup-menu foreground and background colors from 0 through 15.
Syntax: MENUCOLOR=textcolor[,backgroundcolor]
@MENUDEFAULT
Selects the default startup-menu block and optional 0-to-90-second timeout.
Syntax: MENUDEFAULT=blockname[,timeout]
@MENUITEM
Adds a selectable configuration block to a CONFIG.SYS menu.
Syntax: MENUITEM=blockname[,menu text]
@MKDIR
Creates a directory.
Syntax: MKDIR [drive:]path
@MIRROR
Records disk and deletion information used by UNFORMAT and UNDELETE.
Syntax: MIRROR [drive: [...]] [/1] or MIRROR /Tdrive[-entries] or MIRROR /U or MIRROR /PARTN
@MODE
Configures system devices.
Syntax: MODE device parameters
@MORE
Displays output one screen at a time.
Syntax: MORE [drive:][path]filename or command | MORE
@MOVE
Moves files, or renames files and directories.
Syntax: MOVE [/Y | /-Y] source [source ...] target
@MSCDEX
Installs the CD-ROM redirector for an external device driver.
Syntax: MSCDEX [/E/K/S/V] [/D:driver ...] [/L:letter] [/M:buffers]
The current implementation provides installation and the core INT 2Fh discovery
API. ISO 9660 file access and media-control calls are not yet implemented.
@MSD
Displays operating-system, computer, memory, video, disk, IRQ, driver, and network information.
Syntax: MSD [/B] [/I] [/F [filename]] [/P] [/S]
/B uses the text-only display, /I skips extended probing, /F writes a report,
/P sends a report to the printer, and /S selects the complete report.
@NLSFUNC
Loads country-specific information.
Syntax: NLSFUNC [[drive:][path]country-file]
@PATH
Displays or sets the executable search path.
Syntax: PATH [[drive:]path[;...]]
@PAUSE
Suspends batch processing until a key is pressed.
Syntax: PAUSE
@PRINT
Prints a text file in the background.
Syntax: PRINT [/D:device] [/B:size] [/U:ticks] [/M:ticks] [/S:ticks] [/Q:size] files
@POWER
Reports or changes the resident POWER.EXE driver's conservation policy.
Install it first with DEVICE=POWER.EXE in CONFIG.SYS.
Syntax: POWER [ADV[:MAX|REG|MIN]|STD|OFF]
ADV uses software idle detection. STD uses the computer's APM support.
@PROMPT
Changes the command prompt.
Syntax: PROMPT [text]
@RD
Removes an empty directory.
Syntax: RD [drive:]path
@RECOVER
Recovers readable information from a damaged disk or file.
Syntax: RECOVER drive: or RECOVER [drive:][path]filename
@REN
Renames files.
Syntax: REN [drive:][path]filename1 filename2
@RENAME
Renames files.
Syntax: RENAME [drive:][path]filename1 filename2
@REPLACE
Replaces files in a destination directory.
Syntax: REPLACE [drive:][path]filename [drive:][path] [/A] [/P] [/R] [/S] [/W] [/U]
@RESTORE
Restores files created by BACKUP.
Syntax: RESTORE drive1: drive2:[path][filename] [options]
@RMDIR
Removes an empty directory.
Syntax: RMDIR [drive:]path
@SCANDISK
Checks FAT12 and FAT16 disks and repairs allocation errors.
Syntax: SCANDISK [drive:] [/ALL] [/AUTOFIX] [/CHECKONLY] [/CUSTOM]
                [/FRAGMENT] [/MONO] [/NOSAVE] [/NOSUMMARY] [/SURFACE] [/UNDO]
/CHECKONLY never repairs; /AUTOFIX repairs without prompting. /NOSAVE frees
lost chains instead of saving FILEnnnn.CHK files. /SURFACE reads data clusters.
With /CUSTOM, environment and repair policy come from SCANDISK.INI.
@SET
Displays, sets, or removes environment variables.
Syntax: SET [variable=[string]]
@SETVER
Displays or changes the DOS version table.
Syntax: SETVER [filename n.nn | filename /DELETE]
@SHARE
Installs file sharing and locking support.
Syntax: SHARE [/F:space] [/L:locks]
@SMARTDRV
Configures and reports the resident disk cache.
Syntax: SMARTDRV [/X] [[drive[+|-]]...] [/U] [/C|/R] [/F|/N] [/L]
                [/V|/Q|/S] [InitCacheSize [WinCacheSize]]
                [/E:ElementSize] [/B:BufferSize]
A drive letter enables read caching, + enables reads and delayed writes, and
- disables caching. /C flushes delayed writes; /X and /N disable them.
@SHIFT
Shifts replaceable batch parameters.
Syntax: SHIFT
@SORT
Sorts input and writes the result.
Syntax: SORT [/R] [/+n] [< input] [> output]
@SUBST
Associates a path with a drive letter.
Syntax: SUBST drive: [drive:]path or SUBST drive: /D
@SUBMENU
Adds a nested menu block; missing menu blocks are not displayed.
Syntax: SUBMENU=blockname[,menu text]
@SYS
Transfers system files and writes a boot sector.
Syntax: SYS [drive1:][path] drive2:
@TIME
Displays or sets the system time.
Syntax: TIME [time]
@TREE
Graphically displays a directory structure.
Syntax: TREE [drive:][path] [/F] [/A]
@TYPE
Displays a text file.
Syntax: TYPE [drive:][path]filename
@UNDELETE
Restores files deleted with DEL.
Syntax: UNDELETE [[drive:][path]filename] [/LIST|/ALL] [/DOS|/DT]
@UNFORMAT
Restores formatted disks or saved hard-disk partition tables.
Syntax: UNFORMAT drive: [/J] or UNFORMAT drive: [/U] [/L] [/TEST] [/P] or UNFORMAT /PARTN [/L]
@VER
Displays the MS-DOS version.
Syntax: VER
@VERIFY
Controls verification of disk writes.
Syntax: VERIFY [ON|OFF]
@VOL
Displays a disk volume label and serial number.
Syntax: VOL [drive:]
@XCOPY
Copies files and directory trees.
Syntax: XCOPY source [destination] [/A|/M] [/D:date] [/P] [/S] [/E] [/V] [/W] [/Y|/-Y]
Prompts before replacing files unless /Y or COPYCMD=/Y selects automatic replacement.
Hidden and system files are not copied.
